== B. GB2 worst-case factor F = total/K, and analytic instances ==
   F_sum = 1 + 1/c + n0/log2(1/gamma) (the note), F_max = max(1 + 1/c, n0/log2(1/gamma)) (also valid);
   at gamma = log2(n0)/n0 and at the gamma minimizing F_max; the scan pays n0 per bit, S,U,S,H 2 n0.
   | n0 | F_sum(note gamma) | F_max(note gamma) | phase-1 part 1+1/c | best gamma | F_max(best) | n0 | 2 n0 |
   |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
   | 16 | 11.41 | 8.00 | 3.41 | 0.139 | 5.62 | 16 | 32 |
   | 20 | 12.90 | 9.05 | 3.85 | 0.118 | 6.50 | 20 | 40 |
   | 30 | 16.37 | 11.49 | 4.88 | 0.088 | 8.55 | 30 | 60 |
   | 40 | 19.60 | 13.75 | 5.85 | 0.071 | 10.46 | 40 | 80 |
   | 64 | 26.78 | 18.74 | 8.04 | 0.049 | 14.73 | 64 | 128 |
   | 1024 | 224.97 | 153.34 | 71.63 | 0.005 | 134.89 | 1024 | 2048 |
   Tightness (silent class with known insight value, eta = 1/2, adversarial phase-2 order, human with an
   insight in every problem): cost n0 per insight, K = log2(2 n0) bits per insight:
     n0 = 16: actual Q/K = 3.20; GB2 bound F_sum = 11.41 (ratio 0.28), F_max = 8.00 (ratio 0.40)
     n0 = 64: actual Q/K = 9.14; GB2 bound F_sum = 26.78 (ratio 0.34), F_max = 18.74 (ratio 0.49)
     n0 = 1024: actual Q/K = 93.09; GB2 bound F_sum = 224.97 (ratio 0.41), F_max = 153.34 (ratio 0.61)
   The scan's n0 K is attained: one fair coin per problem at step n0-1, human never the tie-break:
     scan Q = n0 per bit; B_gamma (gamma <= 1/2) Q = 1 per bit.  So GB2 does improve the worst case.

